<template><div class="site"><SiteHeader/><main class="guide content-width"><header class="guide-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p><h1>RAID OPS privacy</h1><p>Last updated: November 26, 2026</p></header><article class="prose"><h2>Website operator</h2><p>This website and its browser game are operated under the name {{ SITE_OWNER.operatorName }}.</p><h2>Game progress and preferences</h2><p>RAID OPS uses local storage in your browser to keep unlocked weapons, weapon research, mission records, tutorial preferences, audio settings and one continuing battlefield save. That save includes position, health, enemies, supplies, objectives and equipment state. Quick start does not replace the continuing save. You do not need a game account to play. This version does not upload that local save to an account server or synchronize it between devices.</p><h2>Removing your save</h2><p>You can remove the stored information by clearing site data for runandgun.games in your browser settings. This also removes the progress and preferences saved on that browser. A save on another domain, including a private preview, is separate and is not automatically transferred here.</p><h2>Requests to the website</h2><p>Your browser requests game code, images, fonts and audio from the site. Hosting infrastructure may process ordinary request information, such as an IP address, requested address and browser information, to deliver the files and operate the service. That information is separate from the locally stored game save.</p><h2>Analytics and advertising</h2><p>RAID OPS sends first-party usage statistics through /e on this domain to our statistics service. Reports include page paths, referring domains, campaign and mission events, operative choices, and whether active play reached one or five minutes. Paused time and the title-screen demo do not count as active play. Browser language, device, operating system, approximate country and automation indicators help interpret traffic.</p><p>Analytics uses no cookies or persistent browser identifier. Each page view receives a random identifier held only in memory. The service derives a daily visitor identifier from the date, IP address and browser information using a server secret; it does not retain the raw IP address in the analytics table. The identifier changes daily. Referrer query strings, complete saves, player positions and health are not sent. Detailed analytics records are retained for up to 400 days. Infrastructure access logs may follow separate retention settings. No third-party advertising scripts are included.</p><h2>Browser controls</h2><p>Private browsing or browser storage restrictions may prevent saves from persisting. The game can still start without a stored save, but you should not expect your progress to remain after that browser session ends. Audio and reduced-motion preferences can also be adjusted within the game.</p></article></main><SiteFooter/></div></template>
